From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:43:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 095/202] [ae-patch] Edit a global policy's parameters on the
 Global Policies page

Each stored global policy whose registry entry is a factory with parameters
gets an Edit button (Tabler pencil) beside its switch. It opens the add
dialog in an edit mode: no picker, the name fixed, every parameter prefilled
from the stored factory_params, and Save sends PATCH /v1/policies/{id} with
the new params, which the previous patch checks and builds before saving.

The form's strings cannot carry every stored value back (an empty list,
numbers or objects in a list, an item with a comma), so a field the admin did
not change keeps its stored value exactly, as do stored keys the form does
not show. A changed field takes the dialog's value, and a cleared one is left
out, so the factory's default applies. The add, update and delete hooks throw
the server's reason through apiErrorFromResponse, so the dialog shows why a
save or an add was refused.

The logic lives in new files (web/src/lib/aePolicyEdit.ts for the form values,
the saved params and the editable rule; web/src/components/AePolicyEditButton.tsx);
the page gains an optional `editing` prop on AddDefaultPolicyDialog, and
useUpdateDefaultPolicy sends only the fields it is given, so the switch still
sends exactly {enabled}.
